A||||11||fierobob88||borla exhaust||||1||
Z||000000||fierobob88||04-11-2001||02:36 PM||||So I have noticed that fieroparts.com sells a borla cat-back exhaust for the fieros.  It shows a dyno showing 7 hp gained.  I was wandering if anyone here has that exhaust, or thinks it is worth the money for it ($535)||||reg||1
Z||000001||fyerstarter||04-11-2001||04:06 PM||||Option 1:<P>-80 Series Flowy $80 (www.summitracing.com)<BR>-Exhaust Tips $80<BR>-Custom work to accomodate the oversize muffler $100<P>Total: $260<P>Option 2: <P>-Chris West Custom Fit Flowmaster $140 <A HREF="http://www.cmwestco.com)" TARGET=_blank>www.cmwestco.com)</A> <BR>-Chris West 2.5" piping $175<BR>-Exhaust Tips $80<BR>-Labor at your local muffler shop $75<P>Total: $470<P>Option 3:<P>-Borla Cat back exhaust system $535<P><BR>I think you can expect to see the same performance gains and sound characteristics from all these setups. Just depends on how much you really want to spend.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||04-11-2001||04:34 PM||||Spintech 331SC or 333SC Muffler. Fits the stock location, 2.5" in dual 2" or 2.5" out. $140 out the door including CA sales tax. No sales tax outside CA. Quieter and better flow than LoudMasters.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-11-2001||08:00 PM||||I replaced the cat when I put on the Borla I bought from Tim.  It sounds great, and I can get 30+ mpg over the road.  I bought it not for the performance, but for improved breathing and being made of stainless, it should last for a couple of decades.<P>I cannot believe that anyone can see any performance difference with an additional 7 hp in their car. But again, I don't use the car for drag racing or road racing.||||reg||3
Z||000004||Black88GT||04-11-2001||08:30 PM||||The thing that sets the Borla appart from the flow masters and all the other setups is the 304 stainless steel construction.  The Mustang guys around here with flowmasters replace them ever couple years or so due to rust/corrosion.<P>So yeah you might pay $550 for the Borla initially, but in the long run 304 stainless always wins.<P>just my 2 cents <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">    <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||04-12-2001||05:34 AM||||I went slightly different route since in California we don't get weather.<P>Welding Works custom built a 2 1/2 inch mandrel bent exhaust. <BR>Cost: Around $200<P>2 Megs round chrome 4 1/2 inch exhaust tips with resonators. <BR>Cost: $50 (4 years ago.)<P>Rumbling sound that a V6 with a big cam makes that no Honda will ever sound like. Cost: Priceless.<P>BTW, how wide are the Borla pipes?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||04-12-2001||09:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by terryk:<BR><B>Spintech 331SC or 333SC Muffler. Fits the stock location, 2.5" in dual 2" or 2.5" out. $140 out the door including CA sales tax. No sales tax outside CA. Quieter and better flow than LoudMasters.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>How does the Spintech compare to the factory muffler in noise level and sound quality?  I definatley wouldn't want my Formula any quieter, but I'm not looking to rattle building either.  I take it the 331SC has the 2" outlets and the 333SC has the 2.5"?||||reg||1
Z||000007||BAM-BAM||04-12-2001||10:10 AM||||  Above all, don't forget, Borla has a 100,000,000 mile warrenty against failure. Just an interesting thought.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Knowledge is POWER!<BR>That is why the ignorant remain Weak!||||reg||1
Z||000008||terryk||04-12-2001||11:14 AM||||The Spintech is somewhat more throaty, certainly not quieter, but certainly not like a LoudMaster. I've only heard one Borla but not on a Fiero. No interior resonance, but it does have a peak around 2400 RPM on my 3800SC. I'm running the 331SC with 2.5" in and dual 2" out to keep it quiet. Backpressure is very low (under 3 PSI at 11 PSI of boost and 6000 RPM).<P>I figure this Spintech will last longer than the space frame. It's not a cheap muffler by any means. Very solid.<P>I think it's a far better deal than the Borla or Flowmaster. You can get it in a couple of days too.<P>If you call Spintech and tell them you want something different they will basically build what you want. The 33X housing is the one that fits in the stock space. <P>If you go with a 2.5" exhaust it gets tight trying to bend the pipes to fit especially around the muffler springs (see, there is such a thing!). The outlet pipes are no problem. The shop will moan a bit though.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||04-12-2001||12:28 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.brullenexhaust.com" TARGET=_blank>www.brullenexhaust.com</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> mmmm... <P><BR>i sent ya an e-mail..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 04-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||Formula88||04-12-2001||02:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BAM-BAM:<BR><B>  Above all, don't forget, Borla has a 100,000,000 mile warrenty against failure. Just an interesting thought.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, Borla has a million mile warranty, not 100 Million.  But call and ask them after you put the first million on.  They may extend it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
